@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] review-bot-handle-list
An eligible request line MUST start with at most three spaces followed by `r?` and a space or tab.
Its handle list MUST contain only consecutive whitespace-separated GitHub user mentions or bare
`cc`, matched case-insensitively, and MUST end at the first other token. Only `cc` in that list
requests a contract review.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] review-bot-markdown-exclusions
Request detection MUST exclude explicit quote lines, simple fenced blocks, indented code, and
HTML comments. These exclusions are line-based, not full Markdown parsing: lazy quote continuations,
nested code blocks, code spans, and interactions between comments and Markdown may be misclassified.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:architecture] review-bot-output
The review bot emits `pull-request-number` only for a human's eligible request and requests no
review when that output is empty.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] review-bot-dispatch
When a review workflow is configured, the bot MUST verify requester access and PR eligibility before
dispatching it on the PR's head branch with the PR number and original request run ID.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] review-bot-detector-only
Without a configured review workflow, request detection MUST NOT mutate GitHub state.
